---
id: com.example.ride-check
name: Ride Check
version: 0.1.0
---

One Cloudflare Worker that tells a cyclist whether now is a good time to ride: a verdict, the next twelve hours, the
best window of daylight and how much light is left. The forecast comes from Open-Meteo, which needs no key, and the
page is built with DXOS UI.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term       | URI                          |
| ---------- | ---------------------------- |
| `type`     | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`      |
| `feat`     | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`      |
| `scenario` | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`  |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`  |

## Types

```mdl
type Hour
  desc: One hourly slot of the forecast, in the ride's local time.
  fields:
    time: string           # local ISO time, no offset
    temp: number           # °C
    rain: number           # precipitation probability, percent
    wind: number           # km/h
    gusts: number          # km/h
```

```mdl
type Verdict
  desc: Whether to ride in the next three hours, and why.
  fields:
    level: go | maybe | no-go
    reasons: string[]      # one line a rider reads per rule that fired
```

```mdl
type Forecast
  desc: The JSON body of `GET /api/forecast`.
  fields:
    place: string
    verdict: Verdict
    hours: Hour[]          # the next twelve
    window?: string        # start of the best two-hour block
    sunset: string
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Go / no-go
  uses: [Hour]
  desc: The answer first, in one word a rider can read across the room.

  req F-1.1: The verdict covers the next three hours of `type:Hour`.
  req F-1.2: Rain over 50% or wind over 35 km/h is no-go; rain over 25% or wind over 25 km/h is maybe.
  req F-1.3: Every rule that fired is listed as a reason; with none, the reason says the ride looks good.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Hourly forecast
  desc: The next twelve hours as one chart.

  req F-2.1: Temperature as a line over rain chance as bars, one column per hour, wind under each hour.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Best window
  desc: When to go if not now.

  req F-3.1: The two consecutive daylight hours with the least rain, wind and cold, today or tomorrow.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Daylight
  desc: How long until it gets dark.

  req F-4.1: Before sunset, the time left until sunset; after it, the time of the next sunrise.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: The page answers
  when: a rider opens the Worker URL
  then: the verdict, the chart, the best window and the daylight cards show, from a forecast fetched on that request
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: A change ships
  given: the page is deployed
  when: a feature's requirements change and the Worker is redeployed
  then: reloading the same URL shows the change
```

## Changelog

Every change to this spec adds a decision, newest last. See `lang/changelog.mdl` for the attribution rules.

```mdl
decision D-1: The Ride Check template seeds this spec with four features written, each filed on the project's feature map, and asks the assistant to draw it, build it with DXOS UI and deploy it as a Worker.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  why: A deployed page with live data shows the whole loop — spec, diagram, deploy, edit, redeploy — in a way a JSON greeting cannot.
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The template writes the feature map into this text: each feat block carries its status, the three cards that read the verdict's forecast need [F-1], and [F-1] cites the spec that breaks it down. The appendix defines `feat` at 1.1 so those fields parse. Revises [D-1].
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  why: The spec's text is the source of truth for its features; there are no feature objects to file against it.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The appendix's `feat` carries the role, label, icon and hue the software dialect gives it, so a feature is labelled by its position ([F-1]) and a requirement added from its card is numbered after the others. Amends [D-2].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: user:wittjosiah
  why: The appendix replaced the dialect's `feat` without its `label`, so the card took `F-1` for a plain id and gave a new requirement a random key as its label.
```

